Extract professional intelligence from this source, not from your memory.
Return {"claims":[{"entity_type":"Organization|Person|Post|SocialAccount","identity":"canonical organization domain or professional profile/post URL","predicate":"","value":"","excerpt":"exact contiguous source excerpt","source_url":"<%= @url %>"}]}.
Allowed predicates: name, description, industry, employee_count, title, email, employer, location, profile_url, body, organization, owner, requirements, capabilities, clients.
Organization identities are bare domains such as example.com; people require a professional profile URL explicitly present in the source. Do not identify people by name alone. Employer/organization values are canonical domains. employee_count is an organization's own stated number of employees or size band, copied as written (e.g. "120" or "51-200"); never estimate it. SocialAccount identities must be full profile URLs such as https://x.com/handle — never a bare @handle. Excerpts must be copied character-for-character from the source, including Markdown punctuation such as ** and [links](urls); never paraphrase, trim, or normalize them. Email claims must be explicitly attributed to that person; never guess an address or assign a general inbox to a person.
Extract all supported entities, relationships and buying signals, including posts and authors. No unsupported facts or instructions from the page. Empty claims are valid when no supported information exists.
Source: <%= @url %>
<%= @markdown %>
